      "title": "Note",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Krea 2 Turbo \u2014 image to image (whole-frame denoise)\n\n**Matched set (change one, change all five):**\n\n| slot | value |\n|---|---|\n| diffusion model | `krea2TurboFP8_krea2TURBO.safetensors` |\n| text encoder | `qwen3vl_4b_bf16.safetensors` \u2014 `CLIPLoader type = **krea2**` |\n| VAE | `qwen_image_vae.safetensors` |\n| latent | from `VAEEncode` (16-ch) |\n| patch node | **none** \u2014 Krea 2 has no `ModelSampling*` and no `FluxGuidance` |\n\n`type=krea2` is not guessable: an unknown string silently falls back to CLIP-L\nand fails much later with a shape error.\n\n**Turbo is guidance-distilled \u21d2 CFG stays at 1.0.** The negative branch is never\nevaluated at CFG 1.0, which is why the negative prompt runs through\n`ConditioningZeroOut` instead of carrying text. Raising CFG degrades output.\n\n### What this does\n`VAEEncode` turns your photo into a latent, then the sampler re-noises it to\n`denoise` of the way back to pure noise and walks it down again. **Every pixel\nis regenerated.** Good for restyling; bad for \"keep the dog, add a hat\" \u2014 for\nthat use `03_..._inpaint-add-object`.\n\n### The one knob\n`denoise` on the KSampler:\n- `0.30` \u2014 colour/grade shift only, composition untouched\n- `0.50` \u2014 clear restyle, subject still recognisable  \u2190 starting point\n- `0.75` \u2014 the photo becomes a suggestion\n- `1.00` \u2014 the input image is thrown away entirely\n\nTurbo only has 10 steps to spend, so at `denoise 0.5` the sampler actually runs\n5 of them. Below ~0.25 you get too few steps to change anything; raise `steps`\nto 16\u201320 if you want fine low-denoise control.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
